\code{query}, \code{retrieved_at} and \code{keywords} come from the attributes
\code{\link[=scopus_corpus]{scopus_corpus()}} attaches, and are \code{null} when the corpus lacks them.
\code{query} is a string, or an array of strings when the records were searched
with several expressions. Author keywords can come back empty under some
entitlements (see \code{\link[=scopus_abstract]{scopus_abstract()}}), which leaves theoryforge's keyword
themes empty whatever the writer does, and \code{n_records_without_keywords}
shows when that happened.

The file is UTF-8, with no escaping beyond what JSON requires, sorted keys,
no spaces between tokens and one line feed at the end, so the same corpus
